<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>What a percentage deductible is</h2>
<p>Instead of a flat dollar amount, a percentage deductible is calculated from your dwelling coverage (Coverage A). On a $565,000 home, a 2% wind/hail deductible is $11,300 — far more than a typical $1,000 or $2,500 all-other-perils deductible. These figures are illustrative.</p>
<h2>Why it matters in Colorado</h2>
<p>Hail is the state’s most frequent large property loss, and insurers have shifted more of that risk to owners through percentage deductibles. Rising home values push the dollar amount up automatically, even if the percentage never changes.</p>
<ul>
<li>The calculator shows your deductible in dollars, the payment after it, and the payment if your flat deductible applied instead.</li>
<li>The table compares 1%, 2% and 3% so you can weigh deductible choices at renewal.</li>
<li>If the loss falls below the deductible, the tool says so — no payment would be owed under that deductible.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Deductibles and appraisal</h2>
<p>A high deductible makes accuracy more important, not less. When a carrier’s estimate lands near your deductible, small omissions — gutters, screens, paint, soft metals — decide whether any payment is owed at all.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the deductible based on my claim or my coverage?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>On your Coverage A dwelling limit, not the size of the loss. Check your declarations page to confirm how your policy words it.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I change my wind/hail deductible?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Options vary by insurer and are usually set at purchase or renewal. Ask your agent what choices are available and the premium difference.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does the deductible apply to each storm?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually per occurrence. Two separate hailstorms in a season can mean two deductibles, which is why the date of loss matters.</p></div></details></div>
